From e29d9dfa00bd6afcb6e58c481e866f34641059c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:49:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Implement player drone and fighter control

Every drone command from the client replied "Drone Control is not implemented
yet". This wires them up and reworks the drone AI:

- Engage, Return and Orbit, Return to Drone Bay (drones fly back and are
  scooped on arrival), Guard, Assist, Abandon, Reconnect to Lost Drones.
- Drones look up their controlling ship by ID each tick instead of holding a
  pointer, so docking, jumping, ship loss or logging off can't leave a dangling
  pointer. Drones beyond control range, or whose ship docks or leaves the
  system, go inert in space and can be reconnected or scooped later.
- Aggressive drones defend their ship from anything that locks it.
- Fighters have no control-range limit, follow targets through warp when
  "attack and follow" is on, and warp back to their carrier when recalled.
- Fighter bombers use missile-style damage (explosion radius and velocity).
- Drone, fighter and carrier skill/hull bonuses applied to damage and to the
  number of drones a carrier or supercarrier can field.
- Killed drones free their ship's bandwidth and drone count.

Mining drones and drone delegation reply that they aren't supported yet.

